Append to a Text File using Python

Aim

To append new contents to an existing text file using Python.

Requirements

- Raspberry Pi 4B
- Python 3

Description

The append mode is used to add new contents to an existing file without deleting previous contents.

- "open("test.txt", "a")" opens the file in append mode.
- "for i in range(7, 13)" generates six new lines.
- "f.write(data)" writes the added contents into the file.
- "f.close()" closes the file.

Execution

Run the program using:

"python3 append_txtfile.py"

To check the contents:

"cat test.txt"

Output

The existing contents remain unchanged, and six new lines are appended.

Conclusion

New contents are successfully appended to an existing text file using Python.
